Yeeny showed up during the endgame of my first ascension, and it was
pretty annoying.  Granted, I was well-equipped, and could melee with
him without getting myself slaughtered, but I couldn't do enough
damage to actually kill him.  I recommend, if you have gloves of
course, the good old stoning approach.  Grab a nearby cockatrice
corpse and stone him.  Wish for one, or reverse genocide cockatrices
(be careful), if there's no cockatrice nearby.  In my encounter, not
only was there Yeenoghu, but there was also two demons with wands
behind him, who started zapping right after I stoned Yeeny.  The
closer one had a wand of death, and the next one had a wand of
striking.  Stoned Yeeny, then the striker broke him, then I stoned the
death-wand demon, striker broke him, I grabbed the wand, stoned the
striker, and walked out easily.  Thank god for that cockatrice, that
level was a miserable 1~2 hours of taking one step, wait, wait, one
step, while trapped in between two undiggable walls.

...

Anyways, yeah, cockatrice corpse would solve your problem.  Just watch
out for the YASD's related to cockatrice, eh?

